  "concise_summary": "PKD argues that his 1981 Holy Week experiences (April 1981) paralleled and verified his 1974 visionary experiences as genuine encounters with Christ's passion, death, and resurrection. He traces a sequence of events—mental exhaustion following the Spinner dream, receipt of a threatening letter, and sudden completion of his binary-switching model of reality—as involuntary re-enactment of Christ's cycle. He theorizes this proves the spatial realm derives from Christianity and represents genuine cosmogenesis where net energy is added to the system.",
  "key_claims": [
    "The spatial realm (freed from temporal constraint) is directly connected to Christianity and the Christian mode of being-toward-death, derived from Heideggerian ontology",
    "PKD's involuntary reliving of Holy Week in 1981 validates his 1974 experiences as authentic participation in Christ's passion-death-resurrection cycle",
    "True rebirth involves net increase of energy in the system, explained only by reference to original cosmogenesis—this is the theological center of the miracle",
    "The binary switching model of reality represents the restored universe as Christ has redeemed it, and this model itself constitutes 'Christ consciousness'",
    "Genuine spiritual experiences occur in springtime because they recapitulate pre-Christian fertility rites now summed up and perfected in Christianity's Holy Week narrative",
    "Involuntary cosmic re-enactment (without conscious intention or understanding) provides stronger evidence of authenticity than voluntary spiritual performance"
  ],
  "recurring_concepts": [
    "The spatial realm (timeless, infinite extension, freedom)",
    "Binary switching system (model of reality)",
    "Christ consciousness / Dasein",
    "Holy Week (passion-death-resurrection cycle)",
    "Cosmogenesis (renewal of world and primordial faculties)",
    "The Spinner (character linked to loss and recovery of vision)",
    "Acts / TEARS / Track A (PKD's fictional cosmology)",
    "The Black Iron Prison (BIP as Empire, our world correctly seen)"
  ],
